# Project workflow

- Read AGENTS.md, docs/PRODUCT.md, and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md before implementation.
- Confirmed requirements and proposed policies are distinct; do not silently
  promote a proposal into a user-approved requirement.
- Use a branch in a separate Git worktree for work. Keep the main checkout clean.
- Use Beads for all task status and dependencies; documents describe design only.
- Delegate bounded independent work when useful; assign disjoint files or use
  separate worktrees for concurrent implementation. Integrate and review results.
- Preserve every persisted writing revision unless explicitly deleted. A restored
  version is a new revision. Never couple a draft's passage to reader scrolling.
- The database owns entry relationships. Obsidian export is one-way, incremental,
  and must preserve external edits as visible conflicts.
- Never commit real journals, credentials, caches, or downloaded scripture text.
- Do not build sync, accounts, sharing, or cryptography in the initial version.
- Record decisions and issue handoffs throughout work, not only at session end.
- Run appropriate checks, export the Beads snapshot, commit, push, and verify the
  branch is up to date before declaring the work delivered.
